{
  "description": "issue #685 (slice I6): a click is host input, not a timed event — so advancing the tick clock with `wait` must NOT fire an on_click handler (unlike `every`, which is tick-driven). The registered handler body (`print \"moved\"`) never runs; only the registration primitive, the wait primitive, and the surrounding `print` appear. Locks the never-fires-on-tick narrowing structurally asserted by the runtime (onClickHandlers is never drained by runWait) so a future refactor wiring on_click into the tick path breaks a test (turtle-engine review, I6).",
